PASS: 24H32 registration uses Apple's audited infra wrapper and stable seven-queue vector
PASS: atomic begin/commit/abort and deregistration retry/quarantine states guard queue ownership
PASS: opaque descriptor tail and private QueueSet/LogicalLink layouts are not guessed
PASS: controller publishes only after registration and opens PCI interrupt gate afterward
PASS: RX sink transfers only accepted packets after both interface and queue registration
PASS: failed local registration rollback quarantines all queue owners
PASS: radio events and power controls flow through the registered infra interface
PASS: obsolete bool registration shortcuts are absent
PASS: RTW88 TX-resume callback wakes all four registered WMM queues
PASS: registration payloads/expansion blocks remain opaque and target ABI declarations are pinned
PASS: native interface uses Apple's 24H32 registration/deregistration wrapper transactionally
PASS: QueueSet/LogicalLink private layouts are not constructed by driver code
PASS: controller commits infra registration before publication and PCI interrupt activation
PASS: 0x130-byte aligned opaque RegistrationInfo storage
PASS: exact 24H32 Apple producer overrides and six-byte address copy
PASS: all unlisted initializer-owned bytes remain untouched
PASS: version/size header validation and clear
PASS: RegistrationInfo buffer is 0x130 bytes and 8-byte aligned
PASS: builder follows initRegistrationInfo(option=1, size=0x130)
PASS: Stage108 registration/deregistration uses explicit queue-owner state
PASS: controller registers and publishes the interface before PCI interrupt activation
PASS: four-entry target WMM queue array is fixed, ordered, validated, and journal-rollback compatible
PASS: target TX action reports accepted prefix; native registration remains fenced
PASS: all nine queue/pool acquisitions are journaled and committed only when complete
PASS: partial and committed teardown pop resources in reverse order
PASS: registration and packet callbacks remain fail-closed

